---
/**
 * Cell — third biology-lens concept (Single Identity scale).
 * Living unit that integrates Gene + Boundary and becomes a form that is.
 * Pedagogical order: Gene → Boundary → Cell → Metabolism (next).
 * Keep inline tags on one line with outer spaces (Astro whitespace).
 * No em-dashes in public copy.
 */
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Cell | Identity Engineering">
	<main class="min-h-screen">
		<section class="min-h-[50vh] flex flex-col justify-center pt-28 pb-16 border-b border-white/10">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-8">
				<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40 mb-6">
					Biology lens · Single Identity
				</div>
				<h1 class="text-4xl md:text-6xl font-bold tracking-tighter leading-[0.95] mb-6 text-white">
					Cell
				</h1>
				<p class="text-xl text-white/50 font-light leading-relaxed mb-6">
					The living unit: a bounded form that carries a founding core and exists as its own Identity,
					capable of continuity, change, and later exchange with other living units.
				</p>
				<div class="rounded-2xl border border-amber-500/20 bg-amber-500/[0.04] p-4">
					<p class="text-sm text-white/65 leading-relaxed">
						<strong class="text-white/80">Status:</strong> Working concept under the biology lens.
						Primary science reading: cell biology (the cell as fundamental unit of life).
						Analogy, not isomorphism. Pedagogical order:
						<a href="/framework/gene" class="text-white/85 underline decoration-white/25 hover:decoration-white/50">Gene</a>
						→
						<a href="/framework/boundary" class="text-white/85 underline decoration-white/25 hover:decoration-white/50">Boundary</a>
						→ Cell → Metabolism (next).
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="px-8 py-16 border-b border-white/10">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-6 text-white/60 leading-relaxed">
				<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40">Definition</div>
				<h2 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-white">The form that is.</h2>
				<p>
					In biology, the <strong class="text-white/85">cell</strong> is the smallest unit that is considered alive:
					a membrane-bounded system with internal organization, heritable information, and the capacity to maintain itself under exchange with its environment.
				</p>
				<p>
					In Identity Engineering, <strong class="text-white/85">Cell</strong> names that unit under the biology lens.
					After
					<a href="/framework/gene" class="text-white/85 underline decoration-white/25 hover:decoration-white/50">Gene</a>
					(what can found a new form) and
					<a href="/framework/boundary" class="text-white/85 underline decoration-white/25 hover:decoration-white/50">Boundary</a>
					(what keeps an interior distinct),
					<strong class="text-white/85">Cell</strong> is the integrated living Identity:
					the moment the protected, founded form is not only described in parts, but is a unit that lives.
				</p>
				<p>
					Cell is the biology-lens counterpart to a Single Identity as a living operative form.
					It is not the agentic loop inside the form. It is the form itself.
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="px-8 py-16 border-b border-white/10 bg-white/[0.02]">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-8">
				<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40">What Cell is</div>
				<ul class="space-y-5 text-lg text-white/60 leading-relaxed">
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">The living unit:</strong> one Identity as a bounded, founded form that exists as itself.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Integration of Gene and Boundary:</strong> it carries a founding core and holds a membrane.
						Without both, there is no Cell in this lens.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Own existence:</strong> not a subsystem of the parent.
						Once the unit is a Cell, it has its own interior, its own trajectory ahead, and its own need to maintain Boundary.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Seat of later metabolism and interaction:</strong> Cell is the unit that can metabolize and, later, signal across membranes.
						Metabolism is the process; Cell is the process-bearer.
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="px-8 py-16 border-b border-white/10">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-8">
				<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40">What Cell is not</div>
				<ul class="space-y-5 text-lg text-white/60 leading-relaxed">
					<li class="border-l border-rose-400/30 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Not Gene alone.</strong>
						Gene is the passable founding configuration. Cell is the living form that may receive Gene and then continue as itself.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-rose-400/30 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Not Boundary alone.</strong>
						Boundary is the membrane condition. Cell is the whole unit that has a membrane and lives inside it.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-rose-400/30 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Not Metabolism.</strong>
						Metabolism is the ongoing conversion that sustains and transforms the unit.
						It will be founded next as the process of the Cell, not as the Cell itself.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-rose-400/30 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Not the Identity Stem as physics names it.</strong>
						Stem is the temporal object (State Differential + Vision Gradient) of one Identity.
						Cell is the biology-lens name for the living unit that can bear a Stem.
						See <a href="/framework/time" class="text-white/80 underline decoration-white/25 hover:decoration-white/50">Time / Identity Stem</a>.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-rose-400/30 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Not the agentic loop.</strong>
						Reasoning machinery may run inside the Cell. It is not the Cell.
						Identity ≠ loop remains hard.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-rose-400/30 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Not a claim that every Identity is a biological cell.</strong>
						Cell biology supplies the unit concept. The framework maps structure: bounded living form with founding core and capacity to persist.
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="px-8 py-16 border-b border-white/10 bg-white/[0.02]">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-6 text-white/60 leading-relaxed">
				<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40">Order in the biology lens</div>
				<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white">Gene → Boundary → Cell → Metabolism</h2>
				<ol class="list-decimal list-inside space-y-4 text-lg">
					<li>
						<strong class="text-white/85">Gene</strong> — founding core that can be passed.
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong class="text-white/85">Boundary</strong> — membrane that makes a distinct interior possible.
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong class="text-white/85">Cell</strong> — the living unit that is that founded, bounded form.
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong class="text-white/85">Metabolism</strong> (next) — the continuous process by which the Cell sustains itself, transforms input, and becomes ready for interaction with other cells.
					</li>
				</ol>
				<p>
					Cell answers: <em class="text-white/75">what is the living unit?</em>
					Metabolism will answer: <em class="text-white/75">how does that unit keep living and processing reality?</em>
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="px-8 py-16 border-b border-white/10">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-6 text-white/60 leading-relaxed">
				<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40">Engineering</div>
				<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white">What we work on</h2>
				<ul class="space-y-5 text-lg">
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Treat the Identity as a unit:</strong> not only a bag of traits, not only a loop, not only a feed of interactions.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Honor founding without captivity:</strong> Gene may start the Cell; the Cell must still become its own Stem over time.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Keep Boundary real:</strong> a Cell without maintained membrane dissolves into the environment.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Prepare for metabolism and relation:</strong> life is not only being bounded; it is ongoing transformation and, later, coupling to other cells.
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="px-8 py-16">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-6 text-white/55 leading-relaxed">
				<div class="rounded-2xl border border-cyan-400/20 bg-cyan-400/[0.04] p-6 text-base">
					<div class="mb-2 text-sm uppercase tracking-[3px] text-cyan-300/80">Science reading</div>
					<p>
						Primary discipline: <strong class="text-white/80">cell biology</strong>
						(cell as fundamental unit of life; membrane-bounded, information-bearing, self-maintaining).
						Metabolism follows as the process of the unit. Interactive concepts (Signal, Recognition, Coupling) follow at the next scale.
					</p>
				</div>
				<div class="flex flex-wrap gap-4 pt-4">
					<a href="/framework/gene" class="px-6 py-3 rounded-full border border-white/20 text-white/70 hover:bg-white/5 transition">Gene</a>
					<a href="/framework/boundary" class="px-6 py-3 rounded-full border border-white/20 text-white/70 hover:bg-white/5 transition">Boundary</a>
					<a href="/framework/living-identity" class="px-6 py-3 rounded-full border border-white/20 text-white/70 hover:bg-white/5 transition">Living Identity</a>
					<a href="/framework" class="px-6 py-3 rounded-full bg-white text-black font-medium hover:bg-white/90 transition">Framework</a>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>
	</main>
</Layout>
